Task: Render-loop smoke test — three.js scene boots, empty town ground renders in dev and preview builds

Summary of changes:
- src/game/scene.ts: createTownScene() builds sky background (#87CEEB),
  matching fog, a flat shadow-receiving ground plate, hemisphere bounce plus
  a warm directional sun; dispose() frees geometries/materials and empties
  the graph. Scene type is renderer-free so it is unit-testable.
- src/game/camera.ts: createCamera()/updateCameraFrustum() give a fixed
  orthographic camera tilting down on the town and keep a constant vertical
  world extent across any viewport aspect (portrait/landscape safe).
- src/game/renderLoop.ts: startRenderLoop() schedules rAF frames, reports
  {delta, elapsed} to an optional hook, and returns a stop function.
  Uses three's Timer (not the deprecated Clock) and connects to the Page
  Visibility API so it never emits a huge delta after backgrounding.
- src/main.ts: bootstrap — renderer (antialias, DPR capped at 2), scene,
  camera, ResizeObserver-driven resize, loop start.
- index.html: canvas given CSS width/height:100% (it was rendering at
  buffer resolution, overflowing the viewport — caught in preview).
- vitest.config.ts: coverage now includes the scene module (main.ts, the
  DOM/WebGL glue, remains excluded).
- Added @types/three 0.186.0 (three ships no bundled types).

